### PER HOST VERSIONING

PER-HOST VERSIONING IS A DEAD DREAM. BASICALLY IMPOSSIBLE DUE TO STRUCTURAL LIMITS IN THE FLAKE. ANY CHANGE TO ANYTHING IN THE FLAKE RESULTS IN A DIFFERENT COMMIT. THIS REFLECTS AS A CHANGE IN THE {self} INPUT, WHICH CHANGES THE UNDERLYING RESULT. EVERY HOST WOULD HAVE A VERSION THAT MEANS NOTHING BUT THE OVERALL CHANGES TO THE FLAKE SINCE THE OPTION HAD BEEN ADDED.